\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Cox model for time to incident sepsis (hour-six landmark). SIRS and vital signs carry the hazard, while a single-timepoint SOFA value is \emph {inversely} associated with incident onset.}}{26}{table.5.1}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Discrimination at the hour-six landmark (incident onset within 12\,h) on MIMIC-IV. The full-feature elastic-net nomogram is the statistical ceiling at a single landmark.}}{28}{table.5.2}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Ten largest coefficients (original scale) in the Analysis-1 elastic-net model. Features ending in \_msg are binary ``was measured'' indicators. The act of ordering a P/F ratio is the single strongest predictor (OR 5.46), confirming an informative-missingness signal.}}{29}{table.5.3}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces Dynamic discrimination AUC($s$): one supermodel evaluated at each prediction hour, versus a separate model per landmark. The single supermodel matches the accuracy of bespoke per-landmark models while remaining one parsimonious, deployable object.}}{31}{table.5.4}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.5}{\ignorespaces Pooled logistic model: naive versus cluster-robust standard errors. Ignoring within-patient correlation understates every SE by 2--4.5 times.}}{34}{table.5.5}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.6}{\ignorespaces Operating points: earlier/more-sensitive detection costs rapidly rising false-alarm burden.}}{35}{table.5.6}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.7}{\ignorespaces Subgroup discrimination and calibration-in-the-large. The model performs consistently across sex and age, with no evidence of systematic under- or over-prediction in any subgroup.}}{36}{table.5.7}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.8}{\ignorespaces Cox model: in-hospital mortality by GBTM trajectory class (reference = mildest class), adjusted for age.}}{37}{table.5.8}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.9}{\ignorespaces Logistic model: incident Sepsis-3 by GBTM trajectory class (reference = mildest class). The most-severe trajectory carries an 18-fold odds of subsequent onset.}}{38}{table.5.9}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.10}{\ignorespaces Effect of early ($\le 3$h) versus delayed antibiotics on in-hospital mortality. All four estimators agree in direction and magnitude: early antibiotics associate with approximately 10\% lower odds of death.}}{39}{table.5.10}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.11}{\ignorespaces External validation of the frozen Analysis-1 nomogram on eICU-CRD. Discrimination transports with modest degradation; the gap between frozen (0.686) and internal refit (0.711) reflects population heterogeneity, not model failure.}}{40}{table.5.11}%
